# Day 56 – Windows Server 2025 & Active Directory Home Lab Setup

## 🎯 Objective

Today's objective was to begin building the Windows Server and Active Directory portion of my IT Support home lab.

I created a new Windows Server 2025 virtual machine in VirtualBox after confirming that the Windows Server 2025 ISO worked correctly in VirtualBox. VMware Workstation 16.2.4 had a boot issue with the same ISO, while VirtualBox successfully installed and started Windows Server 2025.

The server was configured as `SERVER01`, assigned a static IPv4 address, network connectivity was verified, and the Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) role was installed.

This server will form the foundation of the Active Directory environment for future Windows client, Group Policy, user-management, file-sharing, and Microsoft 365/Entra integration labs.

