# 🧠 Why a Server Needs a Stable IP

A server providing important network services should have a predictable address.

Other computers will eventually need to locate:

```text
SERVER01
Active Directory
DNS
File Shares
```

A changing DHCP address could cause connectivity and service-location problems.

Therefore:

```text
SERVER01
    ↓
Static IP
    ↓
Predictable server location
```

---

# 🌐 DNS Preparation

DNS is especially important for Active Directory.

Active Directory uses DNS so domain members can locate Domain Controllers and other directory services.

The eventual architecture will be:

```text
WIN11-CLIENT01
        |
        ↓
SERVER01 DNS
        |
        ↓
Active Directory
```

The Domain Controller will use its own Active Directory DNS service after the AD/DNS configuration is completed.

